# fixedbugs, defect 143, panel 185 R1, lane ffi-macro, 2026-10-02.
#
# The repair `ffi_macro_name` names, declared at a wrong width: `hero_SQUARE`
# is the program's own `static inline int32_t hero_SQUARE(int32_t x)`, a
# function, so the probe holds `x: i64` to its `int32_t` and refuses it,
# where through the macro nothing could. The guarantee ends at the function's
# prototype, which the author wrote.

extern "fixedbugs-143-macros.h"
    function hero_SQUARE(x: i64) -> i32  #~ ffi_parameter_type

function main()
    print(hero_SQUARE(x: 3))
